  "content": {
    "id": "p17-q16-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "16",
    "prompt": "The point $P(x,y)$ is an equal distance from the point $F(0,1)$ and from the line whose equation is $y=-1$. Find a formula for $y$ in terms of $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac14x^2$.\n\nEquate the distance from $F$ to the perpendicular distance from $y=-1$, then square and simplify.",
      "worked": "The distance from $P$ to $F(0,1)$ is $\\sqrt{x^2+(y-1)^2}$. The perpendicular distance from $P$ to $y=-1$ is $|y+1|$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sqrt{x^2+(y-1)^2}&=|y+1|\\\\x^2+(y-1)^2&=(y+1)^2\\\\x^2+y^2-2y+1&=y^2+2y+1\\\\x^2&=4y\\\\y&=\\frac14x^2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
